            <ArticleTitle>[Coronary artery aneurysm in myocardial infarct complicated by ventricular aneurysm].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>97-101</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of coronary artery aneurysm in the anterior descending artery of a young female is reported. It was complicated by myocardial infarction and ventricular aneurysm. The aetiology was probably bacterial. Surgical removal was undertaken because the ventricular aneurysm was so poorly tolerated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
